<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Stealing</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 10)
Practising it needs dexterity 30.
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> steal &lt;item&gt; from &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The steal skill enables you to take items from the inventory of another living
being. With this skill you can only steal items that are not worn by the target,
and not money (see <a cmd='#'>Help Pick Pockets</a>). You need a hand free, and you can't 
steal during a fight. To steal from another player, you and they must both 
have signed the book of blood.
</p><p>When you try to steal, your steal skill, dexterity and a little of your brain
and a roll are compared to the target's brain and a little of their dexterity,
and, if the target is a player, their own steal skill. Being invisible helps a
lot. Fail badly and you are caught: the target attacks you and the theft is a
crime. Fail narrowly and you get nothing, but no one noticed. Succeed narrowly
and you get the item but are caught. If your steal is successful you still risk 
that any bystanders see your crime even if the target didn't.
</p><p>If you're good at stealing, this is a fast way to get good equipment, and also a
way to spend some quality time in jail. Not to mention, a horde of blood thirsty
enemies. 
</p><p>Stealing is considered a crime, and few MUD'ers will help a thief in trouble.
Some will not help a thief at all. 
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Filching</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Pick Pockets</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Peek</a>
</pre>




</div>